# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]   (no dollar/backtick in the text)
register_gate "tests/test_landing_record_accuracy.py" "LANDING-RECORD GATE: PASS" "landing record accuracy" "the PR-merge path records only _code_paths-filtered files as landed and is fail-open on transient GitHub or DB errors so the merge handling is never rolled back by telemetry failures" "Locks out round-1 audit defects A4-F3 and A4-F6 on the PR-merge (action=closed, merged=True) path. A4-F3 (transient failure causes full rollback): the old code issued a fresh gh.list_pr_files call OUTSIDE any try/except after the lane release and push record had already run. A transient GitHub error (rate limit, timeout, perm revoked post-merge) propagated up and rolled back the entire event transaction, forcing a redeliver cycle for what was telemetry-only. The fix wraps the entire landing block (files fetch and DB write) in try/except so any failure is logged and swallowed -- the merge is already done. A4-F6 (ledger pollution): the old code filtered only isinstance(p, str) on the list_pr_files response, so docs and lock files (README.md, package-lock.json, .rst) were recorded as landed in collisions_on_main, polluting the ledger with non-code paths that can never carry coupling-level collisions. The fix applies _code_paths (the same filter the rest of the pipeline uses) so only code files reach the landing record. Content-free (path strings only, no code bodies)." 10
